    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25dd9d66_13432c7b",
        "filename": "android/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-17T21:09:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to be duplicating a lot of storage and potentially future bugs if these three slices don\u0027t stay in sync -- perhaps something like:\n\n```\ntype locJar struct {\n   loc string\n   jar string\n}\n\ntype LocJars struct {\n   locJars []locJar\n}\n```\n\nwould simplify things and reduce storage. Then the functions could be defined with LocJars as receivers and we can eliminate the interface.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1297,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1301,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8b07935_c1e81816",
        "filename": "android/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T12:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that struct should not duplicate the information in the pairs. I am not sure that it is necessary to have a locJar struct, parallel arrays should work ok and probably fit better with the external uses that are made of this. I don\u0027t think that pair needs to be exposed at all, except for passing configuration to dexpreopt. The main place it is used is in LocJarsListDiff and I think the pairs can be generated in the body of that method. It could even populate a map[string]struct{} to use to perform the contains check.",
      "parentUuid": "25dd9d66_13432c7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1297,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1301,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b3b7592_eb436f60",
        "filename": "android/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T09:15:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok. Let\u0027s have parallel arrays.\n\nI would not worry about ~2x space overhead though. These are very short (~10 items) lists of bootclasspath/system server jars. The number of such lists in the build system is ~4 (few but not unique). IMO 2x memory here is nothing compared to the way slices are constructed/appended all over the place in Soong. Getting out of sync is a more serious concern (my idea was that coherence will be ensured by the interface operations).",
      "parentUuid": "b8b07935_c1e81816",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1297,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1301,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
