    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "608b8e96_c0c7b080",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-21T12:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a slight change in behavior. The previous code would only mutate the global.ArtApexJars field if it did not have sufficient capacity to hold and additional entry. This change will always mutate the global.ArtApexJars field. I think it would be better if the .Append() method created a new list.",
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c4540b9_f71d78f4",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T09:15:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for catching this! I fixed Append so that it always creates a new list.\n\n(I still can\u0027t get used to Go way of maybe-changing the slice in append. I can understand why it is the way it is, but to me it makes more sense if a function either always changes its argument and returns void, or never changes its argument and returns the new container.)",
      "parentUuid": "608b8e96_c0c7b080",
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97aef082_dcd583ab",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt_config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T20:23:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively, it may make sense to use `global.ArtApexJars.CopyOf()` rather than a shallow copy would reduce the of copying in Append and make it more clear here that `globalArtApexJars` is not being modified. That also makes the Append function much simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "1c4540b9_f71d78f4",
      "revId": "3516e7f517ad048b4b55d5bba9245b923423fc57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
